Independent source review of bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs
2026-10-15

Disposition: no blocking source issue found for the proposed hosted acquisition
phase. This is source-only review, not acquisition, binary, signature, loader,
test, historical-DLL or full-suite acceptance.

Read: the complete new bootstrap, PLAN.txt, the formats loader patch, the unchanged
formats.test.mjs historical bsdtar pin, existing Flow/Vault bootstrap readiness
pin, and root/Archive ignore files. No file in the application or bootstrap was
edited. No binary, network HEAD/GET, process probe, signature/version tool, loader,
test, build, syntax checker or whole-repository census was run by this reviewer.

The tar.exe SHA is identical to the historical formats.test.mjs pin. Both new
asset sizes, SHA values and timestamp/image-size URL components agree with the
identified-image provenance in PLAN.txt. The reviewer did not independently
rehash the identified WinSxS binaries or verify hosted GET availability. Those
remain the acquisition phase's actual checks.

The download sources are fixed HTTPS msdl.microsoft.com Symbol Server URLs.
The implementation permits only its named Microsoft host or a blob.core.windows.net
redirect host, retains only the final hostname, and does not preserve a redirected
SAS URL. Each complete download is limited to its exact expected bytes and a
45-second abort signal. Size and SHA must agree before any image is saved.
Static checks validate MZ, PE signature, AMD64 machine, TimeDateStamp and
SizeOfImage at the expected PE offsets inside the already authenticated bytes.
Version-resource text is labeled expected/uninspected; no version/signature
observation is falsely claimed. Exact SHA binds the full image, beyond the
selected redundant header fields.

There is no child-process import, process-launch call, native image load or
original execution in the acquisition source. It requires hosted Windows,
Node24.16.0, CI=true, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true, RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT=github-hosted and
the named GitHub run/source variables. These are source guards; the actual
workflow/run evidence establishes where execution occurred.

The evidence destination resolves the nearest existing ancestor and requires a
strict child of the real RUNNER_TEMP. The cache is fixed below repo/.local;
the .local and cache directories reject symbolic/reparse links, and cached
images require ordinary-file lstat, exact size, SHA and static PE checks.
Downloads write an exclusive partial only after full authentication, sync it,
and rename inside that private cache. Concurrent filesystem replacement is not
claimed eliminated. Root .gitignore excludes .local, EXE and DLL images. Evidence
receipts contain metadata/identities, not vendor image contents.

The initial receipt uses exclusive creation and sync. Per-asset and terminal
updates use exclusive synced temporary files and rename. Ordinary network,
download, digest, PE and cache failures are recorded as status failed. Storage or
receipt-writing failure can leave the last durable running/acquired state and/or
temporary receipt; no filesystem scheme promises terminal evidence after an
unrecoverable storage failure. Preserve those files and workflow logs if it occurs.

The newly explicit archiveint.dll identity is correctly distinguished from the
DLL dynamically loaded during the old historical EXE-only run. A future loader
smoke/comparison must authenticate and place both images together in its private
oracle directory, record its actual invocation and count it separately from
acquisition. The hosted workflow's x64 Node selection should remain explicit.

Next action: perform the proposed hosted exact GET acquisition, then separately
record the paired-image loader smoke. Preserve failures; do not upgrade these
source-review findings into an execution claim.
